    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "02cf17811914525608c5deb6d6c16fc53c9f07ea5dd36563df27d17270be5ac4",
      "text": "Day 6 · Morning departure from Salta and transfer to Purmamarca (approx. 4 hours), for an excursion to the Hill of Seven Colours and the Quebrada de Humahuaca, a UNESCO World Heritage Site for its wonderful landscapes and a history going back more than 10,000 years, where indigenous fortresses, prehistoric caves, farms and pre-Columbian and colonial villages have survived to this day.\n\nFrom Purmamarca, admire the Hill of Seven Colours and the old Church of Santa Rosa de Lima. The route continues to Tilcara and its ancient indigenous fortress, then past Uquía, whose church preserves one of the most important collections of the famous arquebusier angels. Visit Humahuaca, on the banks of the Río Grande, and stroll its narrow cobbled streets among colonial monuments. Overnight in Purmamarca.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1v28nnxuY_b4MN_reM7Vqwh1l_UEqtgzW",
        "documentSha256": "bf43c2afbe368e6b909ffb3c4ebaeb41a00da5bbd59cee464bc2359e02877669",
